{"id": "live-100", "title": "Deutsche Bank National Trust Co. v. WMN Foshay LP ($51M Foshay Tower Foreclosure)", "category": "lending-foreclosure", "status": "ruling", "date": "2026-04-14", "jurisdiction": "Hennepin County District Court, Minnesota", "state": "MN", "amount": "$51M mortgage; judgment of $42.3M+", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://www.connectcre.com/?p=504290", "summary": "Deutsche Bank, acting as trustee for CMBS bondholders, sued the Foshay Tower's owner, WMN Foshay LP, in Hennepin County District Court in early-to-mid April 2026, alleging the 32-story Art Deco landmark's owner failed to pay off its $51 million mortgage by its May 2025 maturity date and now owes roughly $43 million in unpaid principal, interest, and fees. The suit seeks a court-appointed receiver for the building, which houses the 229-room W Minneapolis hotel along with Manny's Steakhouse, Prohibition Bar, and The Living Room lounge. A Hennepin County judge ruled in late August 2026 that WMN Foshay owes more than $42.3 million on the defaulted loan, and the property is now scheduled for a foreclosure sale on December 18, 2026, with Morningstar reporting that receivership appears likely in the near term.", "judge": null, "tags": ["foreclosure", "hotel", "cmbs", "minnesota", "receivership"]}
